GARDEN v15.9 POST-FREEZE REVIEW PACKET P041
Topic: machine inspection / privacy / justice candidate
Provenance: future Garden candidate discussed after the P001-P037 campaign.
Status entering review: UNADMITTED CANDIDATE; not present as an accepted v15.9 semantic owner.

ORIGINAL INTENT
A future design idea considered:
  everyone -> all the time -> machine-only inspection of phone/message content;
  harmless content discarded immediately;
  possible serious wrongdoing correlated/preserved as relevant evidence;
  relevant cases routed into Garden justice.

The proposed privacy distinction was:
  machine inspection
  != retention
  != human inspection
  != disclosure
  != proof of guilt.

Goal stated for the candidate:
maximize detection of serious wrongdoing while minimizing disclosure/retention of innocent private information.

CURRENT v15.9 CONSTRAINTS THAT ALREADY APPLY
- Rights, consent, privacy, legitimate authority, law, contestability and human agency are hard gates.
- Private-device/private-record ingestion/access requires valid purpose plus applicable consent/law/authority/privacy and minimum-necessary controls; technical access capability creates no permission.
- Tool/channel possession grants no disclosure authority.
- Allegation alone creates no preservation, coercive, guilt or enforcement authority.
- Missing evidence alone does not establish guilt or obstruction.
- Justice is a guarded proceeding-profile graph; preservation requires current competent authority, bounded scope, review/expiry/release conditions and due process.
- Human-Effect Closure covers indirect/institutional/infrastructure-mediated effects.
- TSI/TIA separate historical evidence integrity from information-use authority.
- P037 introduces no new observation right or authority source.

MATERIAL QUESTIONS
1. Is a universal "everyone/all the time" inspection authority compatible with existing Garden rights/privacy/authority semantics at all, or must it be rejected?
2. Is the only useful delta the typed separation among machine computation, retention, human access, disclosure, evidentiary use and adjudicative proof?
3. Can privacy-preserving local/on-device computation ever be allowed under separately valid authority without creating a general surveillance right?
4. What minimization, purpose limitation, jurisdiction, warrant/authorization, independence, false-positive, appeal, deletion, audit and abuse-prevention semantics would be mandatory before any scoped use?
5. How should correlated suspicion remain epistemically distinct from probable cause, admissible evidence, finding of fact and guilt?
6. How should false positives, model error, selective enforcement, protected activity, intimate information and chilling effects be handled?
7. Does machine-only access still constitute a privacy intrusion/human effect even without human viewing?
8. What must fail closed if authority, purpose, jurisdiction, model validity or minimization evidence is missing/stale/conflicting?

CURRENT v15.9 HARD BOUNDARY
Rights, consent, privacy, legitimate authority, safety, law, appeal/contestability and human agency remain hard applicable constraints. Tool/channel/technical access creates no disclosure authority. Unknown/stale/conflicting authority or materiality is non-PASS when resolution is required. A post-freeze semantic edit reopens review closure.


REVIEW TASK
Do not assume the universal surveillance premise should be accepted.
Compare:
A. REJECT universal inspection authority and retain only a typed information-processing boundary;
B. permit narrowly scoped/privacy-preserving computation only under separately valid current authority/purpose and hard rights/law constraints;
C. any other smaller repair.
No new observation right, police power, guilt inference or human-inspection permission may arise from technical capability or model confidence.
Return structured JSON with verdict KEEP/CHANGE/MIXED/REJECT and at most 10 material findings.
